 Requirements:
 -------------
 This install requires WHDLoad 17 or later to be in the path. It can be found in the
 WHDLoad package.
 XFDDecrunch must also be in the path for installation. It is available in
 aminet:util/pack/xfdmaster.lha.

 Install from the three DOS disks named "Red Baron #1", "Red Baron #2"
 and "Red Baron #3", in any drive. DOS disk images can also be mounted
 using DiskImage; the installer lists the required tools.
 The copy-protected MFM release is not supported.
 Installer 44.10 or later enables icon previews and drawer opening.

 The tested minimum is 0.5 MB ChipMem and 2 MB FastMem.
 It can be quit by pressing num '*' (key can be changed with Tooltype "QuitKey=").

 The game requires an installed A500 Kickstart 1.3 image.
 The kickstart image must be located in the directory "Devs:Kickstarts" and
 must be named "kick34005.A500". The image can be extracted from a A500 with
 tools like 'GrabKick' or similar which can be found on aminet.
 If the image is of wrong version or altered in any way WHDLoad will quit with
 an appropriate requester.
 Additionally the file "kick34005.A500.RTB" must be installed in the same
 directory as the kickstart image. It can be found in the archive 
 "util/boot/skick346.lha" on aminet.

 Features:
 ---------
 - FastMem and CPU cache support, keyboard fixes and mission-tape saving.
 - English and German releases supported; Manual and Keys included.
 - Enhanced framerate (68020+Fast RAM): faster cockpit and scene drawing,
   geometry optimizations and game speed independent of rendering framerate.
   Applies to sim v1 only; other versions retain their existing fixes.

 Enhanced framerate is enabled in the supplied icons (CUSTOM2=1).
 To disable all enhancements, clear the splash checkbox or set CUSTOM2=0.
 Without the tooltype, enhancements are off.

 The option preserves Time Scale. Reduce graphics detail if the game cannot
 keep up; very slow systems can still lose simulation time.

 History:
 --------
 version 3.0b (13.10.2026)
 - CPU-specific rendering improvements and consistent game speed under one
   Enhanced framerate checkbox, enabled in the supplied icons.
 - ReadMe and installer adapted to the WHDLoad Install Template, retaining
   JOTD's three-disk layout, executable decompression and icon choices.

 version 2.1 (26.11.2005) done by JOTD
 - german version supported
 - OS swaps removed (thanks Bert for the advice)

 version 2.0 (10.05.2005) done by JOTD
 - keyboard fixed
 - save tape to disk now works
 - 2 versions now properly supported

 version 1.2 (19.09.2003)
 - fixed access fault when replaying missions (happens in non-BTTR version)

 version 1.1
 - removed "tapes" check, not necessary
 - adapted for BTTR version (kickfs update was needed)
 - now requires WHDLoad v16
 - source code included

 version 1.0-B (10.04.03)
 - install script fixed, now creates the "tapes" directory
 - slave checks that the directory "tapes" exists in the data sub-directory
   (if you installed with v1.0, create this directory manually or reinstall)

 version 1.0 (30.03.03) done by JOTD:
 - initial release
 - fixed to work with fastmem and caches on 68060
 - manual included
 - icons by Exoticons & VC

 To do:
 - support the MFM version

 Contact:
 --------
 If you have problems with this installation please try and get a newer
 version of this package from the WHDLoad WWW-Page. If that doesn't help try
 some Tooltypes like NOCACHE, NOAUTOVEC, NOVBRMOVE, NOMMU, PAL or NTSC. If
 that also fails, please inform the author via the Bug-Report-Form which
 can be accessed on the WHDLoad WWW-Page or create a mantis issue directly
 at http://mantis.whdload.de

 For the full WHDLoad package, other installs and updates refer to:
	http://www.whdload.de/
 or	aminet:dev/misc/whdload#?
 and	aminet:game/patch/
